signifies_greatest	one
actual_greater	one
exists_mentally	one
exists_actually	one
known_on_terms	one
self_evident	one
# Aquinas's reply to this objection separates "self-evident in itself" from "self-evident to us".
# The objection itself, though, uses "self-evident" and "known as soon as its terms are known" one way in S2, S4 and S8.
# "Exists mentally" (S7) is used the same way in P5, A1 and A2.
# The step from mental to actual existence is made by A1, which joins different claims rather than shifting one word's sense. So I name no bridge.
